 "pages": [
  {
   "slug": "principles",
   "title": "Principles",
   "html": "<div class=\"tmt-design-docs\"><article class=\"docs-article\"><h1>Principles</h1><p class=\"docs-lead\">Short rules that decide most questions before they come up.</p><ol class=\"docs-principles\"><li><h2>Red is rare</h2><p>The ninja retains its canonical pale ink on a dark tile. Accent red marks keyboard focus, the selected tab and the one primary action on a surface. Nothing else is red-filled.</p></li><li><h2>Status is never the accent</h2><p>Working, waiting, review and blocked have their own muted hues and always a mark and a word (● ◆ ◐ ✕). Blocked is a darker red with its ✕, never the accent.</p></li><li><h2>Corners are small</h2><p>Controls, fields and tags share one radius; cards and surfaces are one step larger. Only avatars and status dots are round.</p></li><li><h2>Real components only</h2><p>A mock is built from the same components the product ships, so a mock is the implementation and review compares like with like.</p></li><li><h2>One family</h2><p>One set of components and tokens serves Colab, Remote, Ops and the blog. Product code adds no colours, radii or local copies.</p></li></ol></article></div>",
   "path": "principles"
  }
 ]
